    "title": "Pulse to decisions/0172: pass it on, protect, real conversations, staff messages and mail as rows, grouped alarms",
    "why": "Jason approved closing every gap found when 0172 was checked against the live site, as one release (2026-11-18, decision pop-up, reviewed by the session manager), functional only: the design session restyles Pulse in its own releases. Member and business Pulse: (1) ↗ Pass it on to a connection, a teammate or any email address (Jason chose email too), always naming who passed it on, email capped at 20 a day; (2) 🛡 report through the existing reports and moderation queue, block (they aren't told), mute (only for you); greyed with the reason where one doesn't apply; (3) opened rows are real: a conversation with its messages and Reply, a feed item's words and link, a left message's standing, instead of the mockup's placeholder; (4) ⊕ adds the Address Book and Keep; (5) on a phone the six icons fold into ⋯; (6) groups you moderate fold into your own Pulse with a Groups filter; (7) a tap in the bell opens its row in Pulse. Admin stream: (8) the staff member's own messages and the mail they read are rows that open in place, with a Mail chip; My inbox stays, pointing to them; an email's ↗ forward, 🛡 Junk, block the sender, report phishing, ⊕ make it a case, the sender to the Address Book; (9) Control Board's grouped alarms as one row opening to each; (10) Previous / Next in the drawer; (11) ⊕ A task for you or a teammate. Also (12) message buttons styled, one status line, From shows the sender (held PR #959, folded in).",
